Article 8 A software copyright owner shall enjoy the following rights:
(1) the right of publication, i.e., the right to decide whether to make the software public;
(2) the right of authorship, i.e., the right to indicate the developer's identity and to affix his or her name on the software;
(3) the right of modification, i.e., the right to supplement, delete, or change the order of instructions or statements in the software;
(4) the right of reproduction, i.e., the right to make one or more copies of the software;
(5) the right of distribution, i.e., the right to provide the original or copies of the software to the public by means of sale or gift;
(6) the right of rental, i.e., the right to license others to temporarily use the software for a fee, except where the software is not the main subject of the rental;
(7) the right of information network dissemination, i.e., the right to provide the software to the public by wire or wireless means, enabling the public to obtain the software at a time and place individually chosen;
(8) the right of translation, i.e., the right to convert the original software from one natural language into another;
(9) other rights that shall be enjoyed by the software copyright owner.
A software copyright owner may license others to exercise his or her software copyright and shall be entitled to receive remuneration.
A software copyright owner may transfer all or part of his or her software copyright and shall be entitled to receive remuneration.

Article 13 Where a natural person, during his or her period of employment in a legal person or other organization, develops software under any of the following circumstances, the copyright in such software shall be owned by the legal person or other organization, and the legal person or other organization may give rewards to the natural person who developed the software:
(1) the software is developed in pursuance of a development goal explicitly specified in the scope of his or her job duties;
(2) the software developed is a predictable or natural result of his or her job duties;
(3) the software is developed mainly by using the material and technical conditions, such as funds, specialized equipment, and undisclosed specialized information, of the legal person or other organization, and the legal person or other organization assumes responsibility for the software.

Article 16 The owner of a lawful copy of software shall enjoy the following rights:
(1) to install the software into a computer or other device with information processing capability as necessary for use;
(2) to make backup copies to prevent damage to the copy; such backup copies shall not be provided to others for use in any manner, and when the owner loses ownership of the lawful copy, he or she shall be responsible for destroying the backup copies;
(3) to make necessary modifications to the software for the purpose of applying it to an actual computer application environment or improving its functions or performance; however, unless otherwise agreed in the contract, the modified software shall not be provided to any third party without the permission of the software copyright owner.

Article 23 Except as otherwise provided in the Copyright Law of the People's Republic of China or these Regulations, anyone who commits any of the following acts of infringement shall, depending on the circumstances, bear civil liability for cessation of the infringement, elimination of the adverse effects, making an apology, and compensating for losses:
(1) publishing or registering the software without the permission of the software copyright owner;
(2) publishing or registering another person's software as one's own;
(3) publishing or registering software jointly developed with another person as one's own independently completed software without the permission of the co-developer;
(4) affixing one's name on another person's software or altering the name affixed on another person's software;
(5) modifying or translating the software without the permission of the software copyright owner;
(6) other acts of infringing upon software copyright.

Article 24 Except as otherwise provided in the Copyright Law of the People's Republic of China, these Regulations, or other laws or administrative regulations, anyone who, without the permission of the software copyright owner, commits any of the following acts of infringement shall, depending on the circumstances, bear civil liability for cessation of the infringement, elimination of the adverse effects, making an apology, and compensating for losses; if the act also harms the public interest, the copyright administration department shall order the cessation of the infringing act, confiscate the illegal gains, confiscate and destroy the infringing copies, and may impose a fine concurrently; if the circumstances are serious, the copyright administration department may also confiscate the materials, tools, and equipment mainly used for making the infringing copies; if the act constitutes a crime, criminal liability shall be investigated in accordance with the provisions of the Criminal Law on the crime of infringing copyright and the crime of selling infringing copies:
(1) reproducing or partially reproducing the software of the copyright owner;
(2) distributing, renting, or disseminating the software of the copyright owner to the public through an information network;
(3) intentionally circumventing or destroying the technical measures adopted by the copyright owner to protect his or her software copyright;
(4) intentionally deleting or altering the electronic information on rights management in the software;
(5) transferring or licensing others to exercise the software copyright of the copyright owner.
Where the act falls under item (1) or (2) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 100 yuan per piece or not less than one time and not more than five times the value of the goods may be imposed concurrently; where the act falls under item (3), (4), or (5) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not more than 200,000 yuan may be imposed concurrently.
